#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:6
msgid "Implementing Unsafe Traits"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:8
msgid ""
"Like with functions, you can mark a trait as `unsafe` if the implementation "
"must guarantee particular conditions to avoid undefined behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:11
msgid ""
"For example, the `zerocopy` crate has an unsafe trait that looks [something "
"like this](https://docs.rs/zerocopy/latest/zerocopy/trait.IntoBytes.html):"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:15
msgid "// Copyright 2023 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:16
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:19
msgid ""
"/// ...\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"/// The type must have a defined representation and no padding.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:30
msgid "// SAFETY: `u32` has a defined representation and no padding.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:38
msgid ""
"There should be a `# Safety` section on the Rustdoc for the trait explaining "
"the requirements for the trait to be safely implemented."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:41
msgid ""
"The actual safety section for `IntoBytes` is rather longer and more "
"complicated."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-traits.md:43
msgid "The built-in `Send` and `Sync` traits are unsafe."
msgstr ""
